    "id": 220,
    "title": "Trips you can save: Add to a trip, Your trips, and a guest's trip on the device",
    "why": "decisions/0174 release 2 (accepted 2026-11-19). A person can now gather places into trips of their own. On a place, a business or an outdoor place, ⋯ → Add to a trip offers their trips (the newest first) and New trip, named for the place ('Trip to Show Low'), and says 'Added to …' with Open it and Undo. Get Local's cards have it in their ⋯, and a ready-made journey has Make it my trip. Your trips (the account's menu and beside the Trip Planner) lists them: take a stop out with Undo, rename, Send to Maps, delete (kept 30 days, Put back). The same rules as Directions: a place kept private, told only, marked closed or with only a mailbox address is greyed with why, never added. Guests keep one trip on the device; signing in moves it into the account. Trips are private and never counted per person. Deleting an account deletes its trips. No AI, no outside calls, no cost.",
